  {"id": "anthems", "question": "Why do national teams line up for songs?", "answer": "Before international matches, each team's anthem is played. It is a proud moment for players and fans.", "followUp": {"question": "Do players have to sing?", "answer": "No. Some sing loudly and some stand quietly. Both are respectful."}},
  T6('corner-job','What does a full back do at a defending corner?','Some teams put a full back near a post to help the keeper, others mark an attacker. Everyone listens to the plan from training.','What happens after we clear it?','Everyone pushes out together quickly, so the other team cannot shoot from the edge of the box.'),
  {"id": "friendlies", "question": "Why do teams play friendly matches?", "answer": "To try new ideas and give players minutes when no trophy is at stake. Friendlies are for learning.", "followUp": {"question": "Do friendlies count?", "answer": "Not in a league table, but they still help a team improve."}},
  {"id": "man-marking", "question": "What is a man-marking job?", "answer": "The coach asks you to follow one opponent everywhere. It is tiring, but it makes their best player's day very hard.", "followUp": {"question": "Should I stick right next to them?", "answer": "Close enough to challenge when they receive, but not so close they can spin past you."}},
  T6('morocco-colours','What colours does Morocco wear?','Mostly red with green, the colours of the flag. When the fans wave them together, it looks like a sea of red.'),
  T6('five-side','Why do you love five-a-side?','You touch the ball all the time and everyone attacks and defends. My son says it is like chess with running.','Is it different from big games?','Yes, smaller pitch, fewer players. You have to think fast.'),
  T6('family-game','Does football bring families together?','Always. Grandparents, parents and kids all cheering the same team. That is my favourite part.'),
  {"id": "shirt-swap", "question": "Why do players swap shirts after a match?", "answer": "It is a way of saying thank you for a good game. Some players keep a collection from opponents they admired.", "followUp": {"question": "Do kids swap shirts too?", "answer": "Usually not, since kits often belong to the club. A handshake and a \"well played\" do the same job."}}
